## Original Content
A wave of major AI IPOs could return significant liquidity to limited partners, fueling a new venture fundraising cycle rather than simply affecting public-market valuations. That capital is likely to flow disproportionately to the largest, established VC firms, writes guest author Andrew Gershfeld of Flint Capital, creating a concentration flywheel that could reshape fundraising, startup financing and power across the venture ecosystem.

## Summary
AI IPOs are expected to provide significant liquidity to limited partners, which could fuel a new cycle of venture fundraising. This capital is likely to flow disproportionately to the largest VC firms, creating a concentration that may reshape the venture ecosystem and power dynamics.

## Key Points
- AI IPOs will return significant liquidity to limited partners.
- This liquidity could trigger a new wave of venture fundraising.
- Capital will be concentrated in the largest, established VC firms.
- This concentration may reshape fundraising and power in the venture ecosystem.


